Don't worry, we can all be satisfied! :) We spoiler seekers can get
the info on the infinite gold spoiler, and yet you don't have to be
the one to give it out! The spoiler you are referring to (which, as
you correctly said, does require at least 1 gp) is an old spoiler and
has been mentioned on this group more than once before. I will give it
away again below:

*** SPOILER FOLLOWS ***

You need: A pet of some "intelligent" creature. For instance it won't
work using your pet dog or cat, but it will work with pet orcs,
centaurs, dragons, nagas, etc, among others.

*Throw* your one gold piece (preferrably more) at the pet in question,
and it will catch it. Now, every time in the future when the pet drops
some object that it has picked up, it will drop that amount of gold
that it has (i.e. around the amount that you threw to it) along with
the object. In other words, if you throw 500 gold pieces to your pet
dragon, if it picks up and then drops some object, it will drop around
500 gold pieces along with it! And yet it will still have 500 gold
pieces on it (you can check this with a stethoscope.) Of course, what
you then do is pick up the gold that it dropped, and throw it back to
it again. Now it will have 1000 gold pieces, and thereafter will drop
~1000 pieces along with any object. This is a good use for all those
extra arrows, etc: close yourself and your pet in a room, and scatter
the stuff on every square of the floor. Note that you can double the
amount of gold that the pet drops each time by throwing what you get
back at the pet until you reach 10,000 gold pieces. No matter how much
your pet has, it will never drop much more than 10K pieces at a time.
Still, this is minor, and a player can easily get over 1 million coins
after just 100 drops. (And of course you can combine this with another
well known spoiler that will give you the "strength" to carry those
millions of gold pieces to the endgame.)

